# Accessibility & UI quality

- Icon-only controls need `aria-label`. Every input has a visible label. Decorative images: empty alt.
- Semantic HTML (`button`, `a`, `main`, `nav`) before ARIA. Headings in order.
- Don't rely on color alone (pair with text/icon). Status chips need a word, not only a hue.
- User text can be short or huge: `truncate` / `min-w-0` on flex children.
- Loading copy ends with `…`. Don't leave a spinner with no text on dashboard tables.
- Destructive actions need confirm (cancel ride, delete vehicle, reject partner). Never one-tap irreversible.
- Locale-aware money and dates (`Intl`). `ar` is RTL.
- Hit targets ≥ 44px on the booking wizard and mobile portals.
